<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cen Peng</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died 35</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century">1st century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cen Peng was a general of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-guangwu-of-han">Emperor Guangwu</a> of the Eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-dynasty">Han dynasty</a>, counted among the Twenty-Eight Generals of Yuntai. In 35 CE he broke through the Chengjia defences on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yangtze-river">Yangtze</a> with a fleet and advanced deep into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sichuan">Sichuan</a>, but was assassinated in his camp by an agent sent by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gongsun-shu">Gongsun Shu</a>. His colleague Wu Han completed the conquest of Chengjia the following year.</p></div>
